.DS_Store

# Real anonymizer rules live in rules/ and stay local; only rules/rules.sample.json
# is committed. The patterns are deliberately unanchored so they match at any
# depth: every <db>_rules.json (auth, users, notifications, and any future one
# such as chat) is ignored whether it lands in rules/ or is left at the repo
# root, so a newly added DB's rules can't be committed by accident.
# rules.sample.json matches neither pattern and stays tracked.
rules.json
*_rules.json
